  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 251 PM CDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nDryer air will arrive from west to east late Saturday night \ninto Sunday though mostly cloudy skies are expected to persist. \nMonday will be mostly dry and slightly warmer with highs in the \n60s to near 70. Another strong short wave will arrive Tuesday \nand Tuesday night. PWAT values will approach 2 inches and \nconditions will be favorable for rainfall amounts of 1-2 inches.\nNote, Des Moines is currently a little over 2 inches from the \nSeptember record for precipitation. This will be approached with\nthe system this weekend and the one early to mid next week. \n\nFor Wed into the end of the week, models are taking turns trying to \ningest the Pacific Hurricane Palo into southwest flow as a strong \nupper level low approaches the Four Corners region. There remains a \nlot of uncertainty here regarding this ingestion and the overall \nevolution of the upper level low but a slower progression of \neverything may lead to more wet weather for Iowa.",
